    "result_text": "That's the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires that a created owner exposes a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`, verified by reading it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it serializes into every owner response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `displayName` in `toOwnerDto` via a MapStruct expression: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`, computing it from the stored names.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor endpoint was needed \u2014 the existing `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipelines both respond through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the derived field flows through automatically. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
